        "body": "Ericsson is a Stockholm-based public company, trading under the ticker ERIC, that describes itself as powering the networks that connect billions. Per its own site, it works across 5G, AI-driven automation, cloud, and 6G, and it frames connectivity as an \"intelligent fabric\" linking people and machines through mobile, cloud, and AI systems. It also describes work on trusted AI for networks, network slicing, orchestration, and Open Radio Access Network (Open RAN) transformation, and it cites AT&T as having laid the foundation for an open, disaggregated, and programmable network through Open RAN.\n\nThe site presents the company's position as one of enabling advanced 5G capabilities and enterprise connectivity that unites 5G, AI, and cloud, with its CTO writing about shifts toward a programmable, autonomous, and AI-native network. It also discusses the role of CSPs in the AI economy and its perspective on 6G.\n\nThe record holds no tracked products, no lawsuits, and no MCP servers for the company. Its profile lists it as a for-profit public company headquartered in Stockholm, Sweden, with CIK 0000717826.",
